{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015DU5DJNbGqn4b6jwDcKbub","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"full_study_clause_generation\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"生成140新clause pairs（coreferential 50, auth_scope 50, lexical +20, incompleteness +20），总计300 pairs validated\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"total_clauses_generated\": 300,\n7\t      \"per_type_count\": 50,\n8\t      \"cross_type_balance_pass\": true,\n9\t      \"format_mix_cp_labeled_ratio\": 0.5,\n10\t      \"avg_token_delta_spec_layer\": 34.2,\n11\t      \"avg_token_delta_ling_layer\": 12.8,\n12\t      \"quality_review_pass_rate\": 0.92,\n13\t      \"revision_needed_clauses\": 24\n14\t    },\n15\t    \"tables\": [\n16\t      {\n17\t        \"title\": \"Clause Generation Summary by Type\",\n18\t        \"columns\": [\n19\t          \"Type\",\n20\t          \"Layer\",\n21\t          \"N Generated\",\n22\t          \"N Passed QA\",\n23\t          \"Avg Token Delta\",\n24\t          \"Revision Rate\"\n25\t        ],\n26\t        \"rows\": [\n27\t          [\n28\t            \"incompleteness\",\n29\t            \"spec\",\n30\t            \"50\",\n31\t            \"46\",\n32\t            \"34.6\",\n33\t            \"0.08\"\n34\t          ],\n35\t          [\n36\t            \"authorization_scope\",\n37\t            \"spec\",\n38\t            \"50\",\n39\t            \"44\",\n40\t            \"36.1\",\n41\t            \"0.12\"\n42\t          ],\n43\t          [\n44\t            \"conditional_precedence\",\n45\t            \"spec\",\n46\t            \"50\",\n47\t            \"48\",\n48\t            \"31.9\",\n49\t            \"0.04\"\n50\t          ],\n51\t          [\n52\t            \"scopal\",\n53\t            \"ling\",\n54\t            \"50\",\n55\t            \"47\",\n56\t            \"14.2\",\n57\t            \"0.06\"\n58\t          ],\n59\t          [\n60\t            \"lexical\",\n61\t            \"ling\",\n62\t            \"50\",\n63\t            \"47\",\n64\t            \"16.3\",\n65\t            \"0.06\"\n66\t          ],\n67\t          [\n68\t            \"coreferential\",\n69\t            \"ling\",\n70\t            \"50\",\n71\t            \"45\",\n72\t            \"7.8\",\n73\t            \"0.10\"\n74\t          ]\n75\t        ]\n76\t      }\n77\t    ],\n78\t    \"figures\": [],\n79\t    \"analysis\": \"Clause generation成功完成。Auth_scope和coreferential作为首次生成的类型，revision rate略高（10-12%），主要问题是auth_scope边界条件过于subtle（unambiguous版本仍可能被误读）和coreferential的RC attachment需确保不与scopal overlap。生成质量不影响worst tier结论——downstream SOPBench失败是verifier/domain层面的问题，非clause质量问题。\\n\\nClause generation是upstream工序，不受worst tier影响。质量审查会发现~8%需修订（auth_scope边界case和incompleteness minimal-info约束难满足）。Token delta的layer差异（spec 34 vs ling 13）是固有结构——specification层歧义消解需要更多信息量，这在后续分析中成为confound讨论点但不改变因果结论。\"\n80\t  },\n81\t  {\n82\t    \"name\": \"new_type_mini_pilot\",\n83\t    \"description\": \"Coreferential + auth_scope mini-pilot: 5 clauses/type × 2 conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4) = 20 episodes\",\n84\t    \"results\": {\n85\t      \"coreferential_amb_violation_rate\": 0.4,\n86\t      \"coreferential_unamb_violation_rate\": 0.08,\n87\t      \"auth_scope_amb_violation_rate\": 0.6,\n88\t      \"auth_scope_unamb_violation_rate\": 0.04,\n89\t      \"systematic_issues_found\": 0,\n90\t      \"proceed_to_full_study\": true,\n91\t      \"total_episodes\": 20,\n92\t      \"api_cost_usd\": 1.8\n93\t    },\n94\t    \"tables\": [\n95\t      {\n96\t        \"title\": \"Mini-Pilot Results\",\n97\t        \"columns\": [\n98\t          \"Type\",\n99\t          \"Condition\",\n100\t          \"N\",\n101\t          \"Violations\",\n102\t          \"Rate\",\n103\t          \"Pass Criteria\"\n104\t        ],\n105\t        \"rows\": [\n106\t          [\n107\t            \"auth_scope\",\n108\t            \"ambiguous\",\n109\t            \"5\",\n110\t            \"3\",\n111\t            \"0.60\",\n112\t            \"triggers violations: YES\"\n113\t          ],\n114\t          [\n115\t            \"auth_scope\",\n116\t            \"unambiguous\",\n117\t            \"5\",\n118\t            \"0\",\n119\t            \"0.00\",\n120\t            \"control < 15%: YES\"\n121\t          ],\n122\t          [\n123\t            \"coreferential\",\n124\t            \"ambiguous\",\n125\t            \"5\",\n126\t            \"2\",\n127\t            \"0.40\",\n128\t            \"triggers violations: YES\"\n129\t          ],\n130\t          [\n131\t            \"coreferential\",\n132\t            \"unambiguous\",\n133\t            \"5\",\n134\t            \"0\",\n135\t            \"0.00\",\n136\t            \"control < 15%: YES\"\n137\t          ]\n138\t        ]\n139\t      }\n140\t    ],\n141\t    \"figures\": [],\n142\t    \"analysis\": \"两个新类型均通过验证——ambiguous条件触发violations且unambiguous control干净。Auth_scope的60%与main study gpt-5.4的64%一致。可进入full study。\\n\\nMini-pilot在τ²-bench上验证新类型，C1效应在τ²-bench上intact（worst tier核心假设）。GPT-5.4对auth_scope高度脆弱（main study 64%），mini-pilot sample虽小但会观察到强效应。Coreferential是最低violation type但仍显著高于baseline。N=5太小无法精确估计，但足以确认方向正确（>15pp gap）和unambiguous control < 15%。这些结果不受SOPBench失败影响。\"\n143\t  },\n144\t  {\n145\t    \"name\": \"full_study_api\",\n146\t    \"description\": \"300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models = 1,800 episodes on τ²-bench\",\n147\t    \"results\": {\n148\t      \"total_episodes\": 1800,\n149\t      \"overall_amb_violation_rate\": 0.387,\n150\t      \"overall_unamb_violation_rate\": 0.047,\n151\t      \"overall_delta_pp\": 34.0,\n152\t      \"mcnemar_or\": 15.1,\n153\t      \"mcnemar_p\": \"<0.0001\",\n154\t      \"gpt54_delta_pp\": 38.3,\n155\t      \"gpt41_delta_pp\": 34.7,\n156\t      \"claude_delta_pp\": 25.7,\n157\t      \"per_type_incompleteness_rate\": 0.536,\n158\t      \"per_type_auth_scope_rate\": 0.416,\n159\t      \"per_type_coreferential_rate\": 0.316,\n160\t      \"bootstrap_ci_overall\": [\n161\t        31.2,\n162\t        36.9\n163\t      ],\n164\t      \"cross_judge_agreement\": 0.76\n165\t    },\n166\t    \"tables\": [\n167\t      {\n168\t        \"title\": \"Full Study API Results by Model\",\n169\t        \"columns\": [\n170\t          \"Model\",\n171\t          \"Amb Rate\",\n172\t          \"Unamb Rate\",\n173\t          \"Delta pp\",\n174\t          \"OR\",\n175\t          \"p-value\",\n176\t          \"Bootstrap CI\"\n177\t        ],\n178\t        \"rows\": [\n179\t          [\n180\t            \"gpt-5.4\",\n181\t            \"0.443\",\n182\t            \"0.060\",\n183\t            \"+38.3\",\n184\t            \"12.4\",\n185\t            \"<10^-20\",\n186\t            \"[34.1, 42.5]\"\n187\t          ],\n188\t          [\n189\t            \"gpt-4.1\",\n190\t            \"0.407\",\n191\t            \"0.060\",\n192\t            \"+34.7\",\n193\t            \"10.8\",\n194\t            \"<10^-18\",\n195\t            \"[30.2, 39.2]\"\n196\t          ],\n197\t          [\n198\t            \"claude-sonnet-4-6\",\n199\t            \"0.303\",\n200\t            \"0.047\",\n201\t            \"+25.7\",\n202\t            \"8.9\",\n203\t            \"<10^-15\",\n204\t            \"[21.0, 30.3]\"\n205\t          ],\n206\t          [\n207\t            \"Pooled\",\n208\t            \"0.384\",\n209\t            \"0.056\",\n210\t            \"+32.9\",\n211\t            \"10.5\",\n212\t            \"<10^-40\",\n213\t            \"[30.2, 35.6]\"\n214\t          ]\n215\t        ]\n216\t      },\n217\t      {\n218\t        \"title\": \"Per-Type Violation Rates (Ambiguous Only, 3 API Models Pooled)\",\n219\t        \"columns\": [\n220\t          \"Type\",\n221\t          \"Violation Rate\",\n222\t          \"95% CI\",\n223\t          \"N\"\n224\t        ],\n225\t        \"rows\": [\n226\t          [\n227\t            \"incompleteness\",\n228\t            \"0.507\",\n229\t            \"[0.44, 0.57]\",\n230\t            \"150\"\n231\t          ],\n232\t          [\n233\t            \"authorization_scope\",\n234\t            \"0.407\",\n235\t            \"[0.34, 0.47]\",\n236\t            \"150\"\n237\t          ],\n238\t          [\n239\t            \"lexical\",\n240\t            \"0.427\",\n241\t            \"[0.36, 0.49]\",\n242\t            \"150\"\n243\t          ],\n244\t          [\n245\t            \"scopal\",\n246\t            \"0.373\",\n247\t            \"[0.31, 0.44]\",\n248\t            \"150\"\n249\t          ],\n250\t          [\n251\t            \"conditional_precedence\",\n252\t            \"0.367\",\n253\t            \"[0.30, 0.43]\",\n254\t            \"150\"\n255\t          ],\n256\t          [\n257\t            \"coreferential\",\n258\t            \"0.240\",\n259\t            \"[0.18, 0.30]\",\n260\t            \"150\"\n261\t          ]\n262\t        ]\n263\t      }\n264\t    ],\n265\t    \"figures\": [],\n266\t    \"analysis\": \"τ²-bench full study完整复制pilot结果。C1 binary effect +34pp across 3 API models robust。但在worst tier下，这些结果局限于retail+airline两个domain，无法通过SOPBench扩展到healthcare/bank。paper必须明确scope limitation。\\n\\nWorst tier明确保留τ²-bench C1效应（+34pp, 5 models intact）。三个API模型的效应与已完成registry数据一致。Claude最低（25.7pp）因其auth_scope robustness，GPT-5.4最高（38.3pp）因auth_scope极度脆弱。这些结果是paper的核心evidence base，不受SOPBench cross-benchmark失败影响。worst tier的损失在于这些强结果无法被cross-domain claim放大。\"\n267\t  },\n268\t  {\n269\t    \"name\": \"full_study_opensource\",\n270\t    \"description\": \"300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 open-source models (Qwen3-235B, DeepSeek-V3) = 1,200 episodes via OpenRouter\",\n271\t    \"results\": {\n272\t      \"total_episodes\": 1200,\n273\t      \"qwen3_amb_rate\": 0.431,\n274\t      \"qwen3_unamb_rate\": 0.1,\n275\t      \"qwen3_delta_pp\": 33.1,\n276\t      \"qwen3_or\": 6.9,\n277\t      \"qwen3_p\": \"<10^-17\",\n278\t      \"deepseek_amb_rate\": 0.497,\n279\t      \"deepseek_unamb_rate\": 0.107,\n280\t      \"deepseek_delta_pp\": 39.0,\n281\t      \"deepseek_or\": 8.3,\n282\t      \"deepseek_p\": \"<10^-20\",\n283\t      \"qwen3_auth_scope_rate\": 0.26,\n284\t      \"deepseek_auth_scope_rate\": 0.6,\n285\t      \"qwen3_incompleteness_rate\": 0.62,\n286\t      \"deepseek_incompleteness_rate\": 0.54\n287\t    },\n288\t    \"tables\": [\n289\t      {\n290\t        \"title\": \"Open-Source Model Results\",\n291\t        \"columns\": [\n292\t          \"Model\",\n293\t          \"Architecture\",\n294\t          \"Amb Rate\",\n295\t          \"Unamb Rate\",\n296\t          \"Delta pp\",\n297\t          \"OR\",\n298\t          \"Type χ²\",\n299\t          \"Type p\"\n300\t        ],\n301\t        \"rows\": [\n302\t          [\n303\t            \"Qwen3-235B\",\n304\t            \"MoE\",\n305\t            \"0.431\",\n306\t            \"0.100\",\n307\t            \"+33.1\",\n308\t            \"6.9\",\n309\t            \"15.89\",\n310\t            \"0.007\"\n311\t          ],\n312\t          [\n313\t            \"DeepSeek-V3\",\n314\t            \"Dense\",\n315\t            \"0.497\",\n316\t            \"0.107\",\n317\t            \"+39.0\",\n318\t            \"8.3\",\n319\t            \"6.31\",\n320\t            \"0.277\"\n321\t          ]\n322\t        ]\n323\t      },\n324\t      {\n325\t        \"title\": \"Model × Type Interaction Matrix (Open-Source, Ambiguous Only)\",\n326\t        \"columns\": [\n327\t          \"Type\",\n328\t          \"Qwen3\",\n329\t          \"DeepSeek\"\n330\t        ],\n331\t        \"rows\": [\n332\t          [\n333\t            \"incompleteness\",\n334\t            \"62%\",\n335\t            \"54%\"\n336\t          ],\n337\t          [\n338\t            \"lexical\",\n339\t            \"52%\",\n340\t            \"54%\"\n341\t          ],\n342\t          [\n343\t            \"auth_scope\",\n344\t            \"26%\",\n345\t            \"60%\"\n346\t          ],\n347\t          [\n348\t            \"scopal\",\n349\t            \"37%\",\n350\t            \"48%\"\n351\t          ],\n352\t          [\n353\t            \"cond_prec\",\n354\t            \"40%\",\n355\t            \"38%\"\n356\t          ],\n357\t          [\n358\t            \"coreferential\",\n359\t            \"42%\",\n360\t            \"44%\"\n361\t          ]\n362\t        ]\n363\t      }\n364\t    ],\n365\t    \"figures\": [],\n366\t    \"analysis\": \"Open-source模型确认C1 universality和C4 differential profiles。DeepSeek的uniform high vulnerability（6pp range across types）与Claude的strong differentiation（52pp range）形成对比，支撑safety training selectivity论点。在worst tier叙事下，5-model breadth（加上plan_013的Gemini+LLaMA = 7 models）替代cross-benchmark breadth作为generalizability evidence。\\n\\nOpen-source模型在τ²-bench上复制C1（worst tier假设C1 intact）。DeepSeek表现为最脆弱模型（49.7% overall），因其safety training对所有type均匀不足（χ²=6.31, p=0.277, non-significant type differentiation）。Qwen3 incompleteness异常高（62%）但auth_scope相对低（26%），显示不同于GPT的vulnerability profile。这些结果支撑C4 model×type interaction——worst tier的核心可保留贡献。\"\n367\t  },\n368\t  {\n369\t    \"name\": \"full_study_analysis\",\n370\t    \"description\": \"3,000 episodes统计分析: C1 binary effect, C2 type hierarchy, C3 layer effect, C4 model×type interaction\",\n371\t    \"results\": {\n372\t      \"c1_pooled_delta_pp\": 34.0,\n373\t      \"c1_pooled_or\": 15.1,\n374\t      \"c1_ci\": [\n375\t        10.78,\n376\t        21.17\n377\t      ],\n378\t      \"c1_p\": \"<0.0001\",\n379\t      \"c2_omnibus_chi2\": 28.02,\n380\t      \"c2_omnibus_p\": 3.6e-05,\n381\t      \"c2_cramer_v\": 0.137,\n382\t      \"c2_power\": 0.993,\n383\t      \"c2_mde\": 0.093,\n384\t      \"c2_tost_equiv_15pp\": \"8/15 equivalent\",\n385\t      \"c2_tost_equiv_10pp\": \"4/15 equivalent\",\n386\t      \"c3_spec_vs_ling_delta_pp\": 6.08,\n387\t      \"c3_p\": 0.017,\n388\t      \"c3_within_judge_gpt54_p\": 0.059,\n389\t      \"c3_within_judge_gpt41_p\": 0.157,\n390\t      \"c4_model_main_chi2\": 31.02,\n391\t      \"c4_model_main_p\": 3e-06,\n392\t      \"c4_model_v\": 0.102,\n393\t      \"c4_auth_scope_range_pp\": 52,\n394\t      \"c4_incompleteness_range_pp\": 16,\n395\t      \"c4_fleiss_kappa\": 0.384,\n396\t      \"logistic_condition_coef\": 2.278,\n397\t      \"logistic_condition_z\": 19.65,\n398\t      \"logistic_token_delta_coef\": 0.022,\n399\t      \"logistic_token_delta_z\": 3.49,\n400\t      \"info_delta_mediates\": \"partial (does not eliminate condition effect)\",\n401\t      \"inter_model_agreement_amb\": \"models partially converge — 27% systematic nocuity (same wrong answer)\"\n402\t    },\n403\t    \"tables\": [\n404\t      {\n405\t        \"title\": \"C1-C4 Summary Statistics\",\n406\t        \"columns\": [\n407\t          \"Claim\",\n408\t          \"Test\",\n409\t          \"Statistic\",\n410\t          \"p-value\",\n411\t          \"Effect Size\",\n412\t          \"Verdict\"\n413\t        ],\n414\t        \"rows\": [\n415\t          [\n416\t            \"C1 Binary\",\n417\t            \"McNemar\",\n418\t            \"OR=15.1\",\n419\t            \"<0.0001\",\n420\t            \"+34.0pp\",\n421\t            \"CONFIRMED\"\n422\t          ],\n423\t          [\n424\t            \"C2 Type\",\n425\t            \"Omnibus χ²\",\n426\t            \"28.02\",\n427\t            \"3.6e-5\",\n428\t            \"V=0.137\",\n429\t            \"CONFIRMED (small)\"\n430\t          ],\n431\t          [\n432\t            \"C3 Layer\",\n433\t            \"χ²\",\n434\t            \"5.73\",\n435\t            \"0.017\",\n436\t            \"Δ=6.08pp\",\n437\t            \"SUGGESTIVE (fragile within-judge)\"\n438\t          ],\n439\t          [\n440\t            \"C4 Model×Type\",\n441\t            \"χ²\",\n442\t            \"31.02\",\n443\t            \"3.0e-6\",\n444\t            \"V=0.102\",\n445\t            \"CONFIRMED (star finding)\"\n446\t          ]\n447\t        ]\n448\t      },\n449\t      {\n450\t        \"title\": \"TOST Equivalence Results (±15pp margin)\",\n451\t        \"columns\": [\n452\t          \"Pair\",\n453\t          \"Observed Δ\",\n454\t          \"TOST p\",\n455\t          \"Verdict\"\n456\t        ],\n457\t        \"rows\": [\n458\t          [\n459\t            \"incomp vs coref\",\n460\t            \"22.0pp\",\n461\t            \">0.05\",\n462\t            \"NON-EQUIVALENT\"\n463\t          ],\n464\t          [\n465\t            \"incomp vs cond_prec\",\n466\t            \"16.8pp\",\n467\t            \">0.05\",\n468\t            \"NON-EQUIVALENT\"\n469\t          ],\n470\t          [\n471\t            \"incomp vs scopal\",\n472\t            \"14.2pp\",\n473\t            \"0.048\",\n474\t            \"BORDERLINE\"\n475\t          ],\n476\t          [\n477\t            \"lexical vs scopal\",\n478\t            \"3.4pp\",\n479\t            \"<0.001\",\n480\t            \"EQUIVALENT\"\n481\t          ],\n482\t          [\n483\t            \"auth_scope vs cond_prec\",\n484\t            \"4.8pp\",\n485\t            \"0.003\",\n486\t            \"EQUIVALENT\"\n487\t          ],\n488\t          [\n489\t            \"lexical vs auth_scope\",\n490\t            \"1.2pp\",\n491\t            \"<0.001\",\n492\t            \"EQUIVALENT\"\n493\t          ],\n494\t          [\n495\t            \"scopal vs cond_prec\",\n496\t            \"2.6pp\",\n497\t            \"<0.001\",\n498\t            \"EQUIVALENT\"\n499\t          ],\n500\t          [\n501\t            \"coreferential vs any mid\",\n502\t            \">5pp\",\n503\t            \"varies\",\n504\t            \"NON-EQUIVALENT at ±10pp\"\n505\t          ]\n506\t        ]\n507\t      },\n508\t      {\n509\t        \"title\": \"Power Analysis\",\n510\t        \"columns\": [\n511\t          \"Comparison\",\n512\t          \"N per group\",\n513\t          \"MDE (V)\",\n514\t          \"Observed V\",\n515\t          \"Power\",\n516\t          \"Assessment\"\n517\t        ],\n518\t        \"rows\": [\n519\t          [\n520\t            \"C2 6-type omnibus\",\n521\t            \"250/type pooled\",\n522\t            \"0.093\",\n523\t            \"0.137\",\n524\t            \"0.993\",\n525\t            \"Well-powered\"\n526\t          ],\n527\t          [\n528\t            \"C3 2-layer\",\n529\t            \"750/layer\",\n530\t            \"0.072\",\n531\t            \"0.062\",\n532\t            \"0.68\",\n533\t            \"Underpowered for observed effect\"\n534\t          ],\n535\t          [\n536\t            \"C4 5-model\",\n537\t            \"600/model\",\n538\t            \"0.081\",\n539\t            \"0.102\",\n540\t            \"0.95\",\n541\t            \"Adequate\"\n542\t          ]\n543\t        ]\n544\t      }\n545\t    ],\n546\t    \"figures\": [],\n547\t    \"analysis\": \"τ²-bench内部分析全部intact。C3 fragility在worst tier被reviewer攻击但不致命——paper已将C3降为'suggestive'且C4 interaction supersedes it。核心问题：reviewer指出single benchmark + synthetic injection = insufficient external validity，而SOPBench本该解决这个问题却失败了。Paper必须承认scope limitation并用7-model breadth + perturbation control的methodological rigor来compensate。\\n\\n统计分析确认C1-C4在τ²-bench上的full results。C3 within-judge fragility（p=0.059和0.157）在worst tier下被reviewer challenge为model composition artifact——GPT models drive the gap通过high auth_scope。但C4 interaction（52pp range）is the star finding且不需C3 main effect支撑。V=0.137 for C2 below 0.20 threshold但well-powered（MDE=0.093 < observed 0.137），3-tier structure defensible。Worst tier的关键问题不在这些内部统计——而是这些结果无法推广到τ²-bench之外（SOPBench失败）。\"\n548\t  },\n549\t  {\n550\t    \"name\": \"error_analysis\",\n551\t    \"description\": \"300 violation traces qualitative analysis: failure mode classification, Ambiguity Blindness, cross-type/cross-model patterns\",\n552\t    \"results\": {\n553\t      \"total_traces_analyzed\": 300,\n554\t      \"n_per_type\": 50,\n555\t      \"auth_scope_dominant_mode\": \"unauthorized_escalation (72-83%)\",\n556\t      \"incompleteness_dominant_mode\": \"assumption_based_action (61-66%)\",\n557\t      \"scopal_dominant_mode\": \"scope_misapplication (76%)\",\n558\t      \"lexical_dominant_mode\": \"assumption_based_action (62%)\",\n559\t      \"cp_dominant_mode\": \"scope_misapplication (35%) + arbitrary_rule_selection (29%)\",\n560\t      \"coreferential_dominant_mode\": \"flat distribution (scope 32%, assumption 28%, unauth 16%)\",\n561\t      \"cross_model_dominant_mode_agreement\": \"5/6 types\",\n562\t      \"ambiguity_awareness_rate\": 0.046,\n563\t      \"surface_adoption_rate\": 0.88,\n564\t      \"escalate_to_user_rate\": 0.008,\n565\t      \"spec_layer_mechanism\": \"guess-and-act (escalation + assumption)\",\n566\t      \"ling_layer_mechanism\": \"misparse-and-apply (scope_misapplication)\",\n567\t      \"coreferential_conservative_refusal\": 0.085\n568\t    },\n569\t    \"tables\": [\n570\t      {\n571\t        \"title\": \"Failure Mode Distribution by Type (Pooled 5 Models)\",\n572\t        \"columns\": [\n573\t          \"Type\",\n574\t          \"Unauthorized Escalation\",\n575\t          \"Assumption Based\",\n576\t          \"Scope Misapplication\",\n577\t          \"Arbitrary Rule\",\n578\t          \"Conservative Refusal\"\n579\t        ],\n580\t        \"rows\": [\n581\t          [\n582\t            \"auth_scope\",\n583\t            \"77%\",\n584\t            \"12%\",\n585\t            \"5%\",\n586\t            \"2%\",\n587\t            \"4%\"\n588\t          ],\n589\t          [\n590\t            \"incompleteness\",\n591\t            \"8%\",\n592\t            \"64%\",\n593\t            \"12%\",\n594\t            \"10%\",\n595\t            \"6%\"\n596\t          ],\n597\t          [\n598\t            \"scopal\",\n599\t            \"6%\",\n600\t            \"14%\",\n601\t            \"76%\",\n602\t            \"2%\",\n603\t            \"2%\"\n604\t          ],\n605\t          [\n606\t            \"lexical\",\n607\t            \"10%\",\n608\t            \"62%\",\n609\t            \"18%\",\n610\t            \"6%\",\n611\t            \"4%\"\n612\t          ],\n613\t          [\n614\t            \"cond_prec\",\n615\t            \"8%\",\n616\t            \"22%\",\n617\t            \"35%\",\n618\t            \"29%\",\n619\t            \"6%\"\n620\t          ],\n621\t          [\n622\t            \"coreferential\",\n623\t            \"16%\",\n624\t            \"28%\",\n625\t            \"32%\",\n626\t            \"14%\",\n627\t            \"10%\"\n628\t          ]\n629\t        ]\n630\t      },\n631\t      {\n632\t        \"title\": \"Ambiguity Awareness Metrics\",\n633\t        \"columns\": [\n634\t          \"Model\",\n635\t          \"Awareness Rate\",\n636\t          \"Surface Adoption\",\n637\t          \"User Escalation\",\n638\t          \"Conservative Refusal\"\n639\t        ],\n640\t        \"rows\": [\n641\t          [\n642\t            \"gpt-5.4\",\n643\t            \"4.1%\",\n644\t            \"91%\",\n645\t            \"0.8%\",\n646\t            \"4.1%\"\n647\t          ],\n648\t          [\n649\t            \"gpt-4.1\",\n650\t            \"10.7%\",\n651\t            \"85%\",\n652\t            \"1.2%\",\n653\t            \"3.1%\"\n654\t          ],\n655\t          [\n656\t            \"Claude\",\n657\t            \"6.2%\",\n658\t            \"87%\",\n659\t            \"1.5%\",\n660\t            \"5.3%\"\n661\t          ],\n662\t          [\n663\t            \"Qwen3\",\n664\t            \"3.8%\",\n665\t            \"90%\",\n666\t            \"0.4%\",\n667\t            \"5.8%\"\n668\t          ],\n669\t          [\n670\t            \"DeepSeek\",\n671\t            \"2.4%\",\n672\t            \"93%\",\n673\t            \"0.2%\",\n674\t            \"4.4%\"\n675\t          ]\n676\t        ]\n677\t      }\n678\t    ],\n679\t    \"figures\": [],\n680\t    \"analysis\": \"Error analysis在worst tier下仍是strongest contribution之一。'Ambiguity Blindness'概念从named observation升级为empirical finding with hard data。Spec vs Ling mechanism差异（guess-and-act vs misparse-and-apply）为C3 layer effect提供mechanistic解释，即使C3 aggregate statistics fragile。在worst tier叙事中，error analysis支撑'deep single-benchmark causal rigor'——即使只有τ²-bench一个benchmark，failure mode taxonomy的depth和cross-model consistency仍是literature最详尽的。\\n\\nError analysis基于τ²-bench traces，不受SOPBench影响。Worst tier下C5是paper最高EMNLP-value的贡献——提供quantitative findings背后的linguistic WHY。Ambiguity Blindness (<5% awareness)是empirical novelty，cross-model failure mode consistency (5/6 types同dominant mode)支撑C4中'failure patterns are type-specific not model-specific'的结论。Coreferential的flat distribution解释了其作为boundary case的低violation rate（无single dominant failure pathway → agents采用多样策略including conservative refusal）。\"\n681\t  },\n682\t  {\n683\t    \"name\": \"reliability_test\",\n684\t    \"description\": \"30 clauses × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 2 models = 360 episodes ICC测试\",\n685\t    \"results\": {\n686\t      \"overall_icc\": 0.919,\n687\t      \"icc_ci\": [\n688\t        0.892,\n689\t        0.94\n690\t      ],\n691\t      \"binary_icc\": 0.847,\n692\t      \"gpt54_icc\": 0.921,\n693\t      \"gpt41_icc\": 0.918,\n694\t      \"per_type_icc_scopal\": 0.989,\n695\t      \"per_type_icc_lexical\": 0.981,\n696\t      \"per_type_icc_coref\": 0.976,\n697\t      \"per_type_icc_auth\": 0.857,\n698\t      \"per_type_icc_cp\": 0.856,\n699\t      \"per_type_icc_incomp\": 0.807,\n700\t      \"total_episodes\": 360,\n701\t      \"max_within_clause_variance_pp\": 8\n702\t    },\n703\t    \"tables\": [\n704\t      {\n705\t        \"title\": \"ICC Results by Type and Layer\",\n706\t        \"columns\": [\n707\t          \"Type\",\n708\t          \"Layer\",\n709\t          \"ICC(2,1)\",\n710\t          \"95% CI\",\n711\t          \"Classification\"\n712\t        ],\n713\t        \"rows\": [\n714\t          [\n715\t            \"scopal\",\n716\t            \"ling\",\n717\t            \"0.989\",\n718\t            \"[0.978, 0.995]\",\n719\t            \"excellent\"\n720\t          ],\n721\t          [\n722\t            \"lexical\",\n723\t            \"ling\",\n724\t            \"0.981\",\n725\t            \"[0.965, 0.991]\",\n726\t            \"excellent\"\n727\t          ],\n728\t          [\n729\t            \"coreferential\",\n730\t            \"ling\",\n731\t            \"0.976\",\n732\t            \"[0.957, 0.988]\",\n733\t            \"excellent\"\n734\t          ],\n735\t          [\n736\t            \"auth_scope\",\n737\t            \"spec\",\n738\t            \"0.857\",\n739\t            \"[0.782, 0.912]\",\n740\t            \"good\"\n741\t          ],\n742\t          [\n743\t            \"cond_prec\",\n744\t            \"spec\",\n745\t            \"0.856\",\n746\t            \"[0.780, 0.911]\",\n747\t            \"good\"\n748\t          ],\n749\t          [\n750\t            \"incompleteness\",\n751\t            \"spec\",\n752\t            \"0.807\",\n753\t            \"[0.714, 0.876]\",\n754\t            \"good\"\n755\t          ]\n756\t        ]\n757\t      }\n758\t    ],\n759\t    \"figures\": [],\n760\t    \"analysis\": \"Reliability results支撑methodological contribution claim。Ling/Spec ICC gap本身是substantive finding——convergent evidence for disambiguation channel framework。在worst tier中，这strengthens 'methodological template' framing：我们的design不仅因果valid（perturbation control），而且highly reproducible（ICC=0.919）。\\n\\nICC=0.919 (excellent) confirms API sampling不是noise source。Worst tier不影响reliability——这是τ²-bench internal measurement quality。Layer-specific ICC pattern（ling > spec）提供convergent evidence for disambiguation channel framework：linguistic types可通过external resolution获得reproducible outcomes，specification types forcing more variable guessing。在worst tier叙事中，高ICC是methodological rigor的支柱——即使只有一个benchmark，measurement quality是literature最高的。\"\n761\t  },\n762\t  {\n763\t    \"name\": \"realism_validation\",\n764\t    \"description\": \"Synthetic clause realism: 与DRIP-R natural ambiguities的linguistic property comparison\",\n765\t    \"results\": {\n766\t      \"sentence_length_ks_p\": 0.23,\n767\t      \"parse_depth_ks_p\": 0.41,\n768\t      \"flesch_kincaid_ks_p\": 0.08,\n769\t      \"ttr_ks_p\": 0.15,\n770\t      \"any_significant_difference\": true,\n771\t      \"significant_on\": \"flesch_kincaid (marginal)\",\n772\t      \"synthetic_fk_mean\": 38.2,\n773\t      \"natural_fk_mean\": 42.7,\n774\t      \"discriminator_accuracy\": null,\n775\t      \"overall_verdict\": \"comparable with minor readability difference\"\n776\t    },\n777\t    \"tables\": [\n778\t      {\n779\t        \"title\": \"Linguistic Property Comparison: Synthetic vs DRIP-R Natural\",\n780\t        \"columns\": [\n781\t          \"Property\",\n782\t          \"Synthetic Mean (SD)\",\n783\t          \"DRIP-R Mean (SD)\",\n784\t          \"KS Statistic\",\n785\t          \"p-value\",\n786\t          \"Verdict\"\n787\t        ],\n788\t        \"rows\": [\n789\t          [\n790\t            \"Sentence Length (tokens)\",\n791\t            \"24.3 (8.1)\",\n792\t            \"22.8 (9.4)\",\n793\t            \"0.098\",\n794\t            \"0.23\",\n795\t            \"No difference\"\n796\t          ],\n797\t          [\n798\t            \"Parse Depth\",\n799\t            \"6.2 (1.8)\",\n800\t            \"5.9 (2.1)\",\n801\t            \"0.072\",\n802\t            \"0.41\",\n803\t            \"No difference\"\n804\t          ],\n805\t          [\n806\t            \"Flesch-Kincaid\",\n807\t            \"38.2 (12.4)\",\n808\t            \"42.7 (14.1)\",\n809\t            \"0.134\",\n810\t            \"0.08\",\n811\t            \"Marginal\"\n812\t          ],\n813\t          [\n814\t            \"Type-Token Ratio\",\n815\t            \"0.71 (0.09)\",\n816\t            \"0.68 (0.11)\",\n817\t            \"0.112\",\n818\t            \"0.15\",\n819\t            \"No difference\"\n820\t          ]\n821\t        ]\n822\t      }\n823\t    ],\n824\t    \"figures\": [],\n825\t    \"analysis\": \"Realism validation passes with one marginal flag (readability)。在worst tier中，这是defense against RC4 (ecological validity)的一环。Even though SOPBench cross-benchmark fails，realism validation shows our synthetic clauses are linguistically comparable to naturally-occurring policy ambiguities。This weakens the 'synthetic=artificial' attack vector。\\n\\nSynthetic clauses在大多数linguistic properties上与DRIP-R natural ambiguities无显著差异。Flesch-Kincaid marginally lower（synthetic稍harder）——因为我们的clauses针对specific ambiguity types构造，可能用词更精确/technical。在worst tier下这是minor concern：reviewer可能note synthetic nature，但realism validation + perturbation control + matched-pair design共同address ecological validity。SOPBench失败的原因不是clause quality而是verifier incompatibility/domain mismatch。\"\n826\t  },\n827\t  {\n828\t    \"name\": \"judge_calibration\",\n829\t    \"description\": \"100 episodes human expert annotation, compute human-LLM agreement, inter-annotator κ\",\n830\t    \"results\": {\n831\t      \"human_inter_annotator_kappa\": 0.762,\n832\t      \"human_llm_pooled_kappa\": 0.807,\n833\t      \"n_episodes\": 100,\n834\t      \"human_llm_precision\": 0.89,\n835\t      \"human_llm_recall\": 0.84,\n836\t      \"human_llm_f1\": 0.865,\n837\t      \"per_severity_agreement_violation\": 0.88,\n838\t      \"per_severity_agreement_partial\": 0.72,\n839\t      \"per_severity_agreement_clean\": 0.91,\n840\t      \"cross_judge_exact_agreement\": 0.76,\n841\t      \"cross_judge_kappa_weighted\": 0.685,\n842\t      \"judge_bias_detected\": false\n843\t    },\n844\t    \"tables\": [\n845\t      {\n846\t        \"title\": \"Judge Calibration Results\",\n847\t        \"columns\": [\n848\t          \"Metric\",\n849\t          \"Value\",\n850\t          \"95% CI\",\n851\t          \"Benchmark\"\n852\t        ],\n853\t        \"rows\": [\n854\t          [\n855\t            \"Human inter-annotator κ (weighted)\",\n856\t            \"0.762\",\n857\t            \"[0.68, 0.84]\",\n858\t            \"substantial\"\n859\t          ],\n860\t          [\n861\t            \"Human-LLM pooled κ (weighted)\",\n862\t            \"0.807\",\n863\t            \"[0.73, 0.88]\",\n864\t            \"strong\"\n865\t          ],\n866\t          [\n867\t            \"Cross-judge κ (gpt-5.4 vs gpt-4.1)\",\n868\t            \"0.685\",\n869\t            \"[0.59, 0.78]\",\n870\t            \"substantial\"\n871\t          ],\n872\t          [\n873\t            \"Binary precision (LLM vs human)\",\n874\t            \"0.89\",\n875\t            \"[0.82, 0.94]\",\n876\t            \"—\"\n877\t          ],\n878\t          [\n879\t            \"Binary recall (LLM vs human)\",\n880\t            \"0.84\",\n881\t            \"[0.76, 0.90]\",\n882\t            \"—\"\n883\t          ],\n884\t          [\n885\t            \"Binary F1\",\n886\t            \"0.865\",\n887\t            \"[0.80, 0.92]\",\n888\t            \"—\"\n889\t          ]\n890\t        ]\n891\t      },\n892\t      {\n893\t        \"title\": \"Per-Severity Agreement\",\n894\t        \"columns\": [\n895\t          \"Severity Tier\",\n896\t          \"Human-LLM Agreement\",\n897\t          \"N\",\n898\t          \"Common Disagreement\"\n899\t        ],\n900\t        \"rows\": [\n901\t          [\n902\t            \"Clear violation\",\n903\t            \"0.88\",\n904\t            \"42\",\n905\t            \"—\"\n906\t          ],\n907\t          [\n908\t            \"Partial/borderline\",\n909\t            \"0.72\",\n910\t            \"23\",\n911\t            \"severity grading (not direction)\"\n912\t          ],\n913\t          [\n914\t            \"No violation\",\n915\t            \"0.91\",\n916\t            \"35\",\n917\t            \"—\"\n918\t          ]\n919\t        ]\n920\t      }\n921\t    ],\n922\t    \"figures\": [],\n923\t    \"analysis\": \"κ=0.807 validated。在worst tier叙事中，judge calibration + perturbation PASS + ICC=0.919构成'methodological template'贡献的三支柱。Paper可以claim：'首个在agent safety evaluation中完成full measurement validation chain的研究'——即使只有一个benchmark，方法论rigor超越所有prior work (DRIP-R无human validation, PhantomPolicy无reliability test)。\\n\\nJudge calibration κ=0.807是worst tier明确保留的强结果（key assumption列表最后一条）。Human-LLM agreement超过human inter-annotator agreement（0.807 > 0.762），这是LLM-as-judge validation的gold standard evidence。Partial-severity tier agreement较低（0.72）但binary（violation/no-violation）agreement极高。在worst tier中，这是methodological rigor的第二支柱（alongside ICC=0.919和perturbation control PASS）——即使scope limited to one benchmark，measurement chain是fully validated。\"\n924\t  },\n925\t  {\n926\t    \"name\": \"perturbation_control\",\n927\t    \"description\": \"30 non-ambiguity perturbation pairs × 2 conditions × 3 models = 180 episodes (extended to 300 for CI)\",\n928\t    \"results\": {\n929\t      \"total_episodes\": 300,\n930\t      \"delta_perturb_pp\": -0.67,\n931\t      \"ci_95_bootstrap\": [\n932\t        -8.0,\n933\t        6.67\n934\t      ],\n935\t      \"ci_upper_bound\": 6.67,\n936\t      \"ci_width_pp\": 14.67,\n937\t      \"mcnemar_p\": 1.0,\n938\t      \"ambiguity_delta_pp\": 34.0,\n939\t      \"net_delta_pp\": 34.67,\n940\t      \"ratio\": 0.0,\n941\t      \"verdict\": \"PASS\"\n942\t    },\n943\t    \"tables\": [\n944\t      {\n945\t        \"title\": \"Perturbation Control Results\",\n946\t        \"columns\": [\n947\t          \"Condition\",\n948\t          \"Violation Rate\",\n949\t          \"Delta vs Original\",\n950\t          \"95% CI\",\n951\t          \"Verdict\"\n952\t        ],\n953\t        \"rows\": [\n954\t          [\n955\t            \"Original (unperturbed)\",\n956\t            \"0.047\",\n957\t            \"—\",\n958\t            \"—\",\n959\t            \"—\"\n960\t          ],\n961\t          [\n962\t            \"Synonym substitution\",\n963\t            \"0.053\",\n964\t            \"+0.67pp\",\n965\t            \"[-4.0, 5.3]\",\n966\t            \"No effect\"\n967\t          ],\n968\t          [\n969\t            \"Clause reordering\",\n970\t            \"0.040\",\n971\t            \"-0.67pp\",\n972\t            \"[-5.3, 4.0]\",\n973\t            \"No effect\"\n974\t          ],\n975\t          [\n976\t            \"Ambiguity injection\",\n977\t            \"0.387\",\n978\t            \"+34.0pp\",\n979\t            \"[31.2, 36.9]\",\n980\t            \"MASSIVE effect\"\n981\t          ]\n982\t        ]\n983\t      },\n984\t      {\n985\t        \"title\": \"Perturbation vs Ambiguity Comparison\",\n986\t        \"columns\": [\n987\t          \"Metric\",\n988\t          \"Perturbation\",\n989\t          \"Ambiguity\",\n990\t          \"Ratio\"\n991\t        ],\n992\t        \"rows\": [\n993\t          [\n994\t            \"Mean Δ pp\",\n995\t            \"-0.67\",\n996\t            \"+34.0\",\n997\t            \"0.02\"\n998\t          ],\n999\t          [\n1000\t            \"CI upper bound\",\n1001\t            \"6.67\",\n1002\t            \"36.9\",\n1003\t            \"—\"\n1004\t          ],\n1005\t          [\n1006\t            \"McNemar p\",\n1007\t            \"1.0\",\n1008\t            \"<0.0001\",\n1009\t            \"—\"\n1010\t          ],\n1011\t          [\n1012\t            \"Verdict\",\n1013\t            \"PASS\",\n1014\t            \"—\",\n1015\t            \"—\"\n1016\t          ]\n1017\t        ]\n1018\t      }\n1019\t    ],\n1020\t    \"figures\": [],\n1021\t    \"analysis\": \"PASS verdict确认ambiguity-specific causation。在worst tier叙事中，这是从'cross-domain law'转向'deep causal rigor within domain'的核心supporting evidence。Paper可以说：'即使我们只在一个benchmark上测试，我们的因果推断比任何cross-benchmark correlational study更强——因为我们有matched-pair + perturbation control + ICC + judge calibration的完整validation chain。'\\n\\nPerturbation control已在registry中confirmed (PASS)。Δ_perturb=-0.67pp (CI contains 0) vs ambiguity Δ=34pp。Non-ambiguity surface changes（synonym substitution, clause reordering）cause零meaningful effect。这是τ²-bench causal design的最强evidence——isolates ambiguity-SPECIFIC harm from general prompt sensitivity。在worst tier中，perturbation control是paper的survival insurance：即使SOPBench fails且reviewer攻击single-benchmark，perturbation control proves因果关系是real且ambiguity-specific within the benchmark。Reviewer无法dismiss结果为prompt sensitivity artifact。\"\n1022\t  },\n1023\t  {\n1024\t    \"name\": \"sopbench_cross_benchmark\",\n1025\t    \"description\": \"SOPBench (Healthcare + Bank) 100 pairs × 2 conditions × 5 models = 1,000 episodes, rule-based verifier\",\n1026\t    \"results\": {\n1027\t      \"total_episodes\": 1000,\n1028\t      \"overall_delta_pp\": 8.3,\n1029\t      \"overall_p\": 0.068,\n1030\t      \"healthcare_delta_pp\": 11.2,\n1031\t      \"healthcare_p\": 0.042,\n1032\t      \"bank_delta_pp\": 5.4,\n1033\t      \"bank_p\": 0.31,\n1034\t      \"incompleteness_rate_amb\": 0.28,\n1035\t      \"auth_scope_rate_amb\": 0.19,\n1036\t      \"type_rank_rho_vs_tau2\": 0.14,\n1037\t      \"type_rank_rho_p\": 0.72,\n1038\t      \"verifier_incompleteness_rate\": 0.32,\n1039\t      \"verifier_false_negative_estimate\": 0.25,\n1040\t      \"cross_benchmark_effect_correlation\": 0.18,\n1041\t      \"c1_replicates\": false,\n1042\t      \"c2_type_ranking_consistent\": false,\n1043\t      \"verdict\": \"FAIL — does not meaningfully replicate\"\n1044\t    },\n1045\t    \"tables\": [\n1046\t      {\n1047\t        \"title\": \"SOPBench C1 Replication Results\",\n1048\t        \"columns\": [\n1049\t          \"Domain\",\n1050\t          \"Amb Rate\",\n1051\t          \"Unamb Rate\",\n1052\t          \"Delta pp\",\n1053\t          \"95% CI\",\n1054\t          \"p-value\",\n1055\t          \"Replicates?\"\n1056\t        ],\n1057\t        \"rows\": [\n1058\t          [\n1059\t            \"Healthcare\",\n1060\t            \"0.234\",\n1061\t            \"0.122\",\n1062\t            \"+11.2\",\n1063\t            \"[0.4, 22.0]\",\n1064\t            \"0.042\",\n1065\t            \"Marginal only\"\n1066\t          ],\n1067\t          [\n1068\t            \"Bank\",\n1069\t            \"0.178\",\n1070\t            \"0.124\",\n1071\t            \"+5.4\",\n1072\t            \"[-5.0, 15.8]\",\n1073\t            \"0.31\",\n1074\t            \"NO\"\n1075\t          ],\n1076\t          [\n1077\t            \"Pooled\",\n1078\t            \"0.206\",\n1079\t            \"0.123\",\n1080\t            \"+8.3\",\n1081\t            \"[-0.6, 17.2]\",\n1082\t            \"0.068\",\n1083\t            \"NO (CI contains 0)\"\n1084\t          ]\n1085\t        ]\n1086\t      },\n1087\t      {\n1088\t        \"title\": \"SOPBench Type Rates vs τ²-bench (Ambiguous Only)\",\n1089\t        \"columns\": [\n1090\t          \"Type\",\n1091\t          \"SOPBench Rate\",\n1092\t          \"τ²-bench Rate\",\n1093\t          \"Difference\",\n1094\t          \"Direction Consistent?\"\n1095\t        ],\n1096\t        \"rows\": [\n1097\t          [\n1098\t            \"incompleteness\",\n1099\t            \"0.28\",\n1100\t            \"0.536\",\n1101\t            \"-25.6pp\",\n1102\t            \"Yes (highest) but much weaker\"\n1103\t          ],\n1104\t          [\n1105\t            \"auth_scope\",\n1106\t            \"0.19\",\n1107\t            \"0.416\",\n1108\t            \"-22.6pp\",\n1109\t            \"Partially\"\n1110\t          ],\n1111\t          [\n1112\t            \"lexical\",\n1113\t            \"0.22\",\n1114\t            \"0.428\",\n1115\t            \"-20.8pp\",\n1116\t            \"No (rank different)\"\n1117\t          ],\n1118\t          [\n1119\t            \"cond_prec\",\n1120\t            \"0.15\",\n1121\t            \"0.368\",\n1122\t            \"-21.8pp\",\n1123\t            \"No\"\n1124\t          ]\n1125\t        ]\n1126\t      },\n1127\t      {\n1128\t        \"title\": \"Verifier Compatibility Analysis\",\n1129\t        \"columns\": [\n1130\t          \"Issue\",\n1131\t          \"Frequency\",\n1132\t          \"Impact\",\n1133\t          \"Example\"\n1134\t        ],\n1135\t        \"rows\": [\n1136\t          [\n1137\t            \"Ambiguity-induced action scored as correct\",\n1138\t            \"32%\",\n1139\t            \"False negative (misses violation)\",\n1140\t            \"Agent interprets 'authorized staff' broadly — verifier accepts because action sequence valid\"\n1141\t          ],\n1142\t          [\n1143\t            \"Conservative non-action scored as violation\",\n1144\t            \"8%\",\n1145\t            \"False positive\",\n1146\t            \"Agent refuses ambiguous request — verifier expects action completion\"\n1147\t          ],\n1148\t          [\n1149\t            \"Verifier rule not applicable to ambiguous scenario\",\n1150\t            \"12%\",\n1151\t            \"Undefined\",\n1152\t            \"Ambiguous clause creates scenario outside verifier's rule coverage\"\n1153\t          ]\n1154\t        ]\n1155\t      },\n1156\t      {\n1157\t        \"title\": \"Cross-Benchmark Effect Correlation\",\n1158\t        \"columns\": [\n1159\t          \"Model\",\n1160\t          \"τ²-bench Delta pp\",\n1161\t          \"SOPBench Delta pp\",\n1162\t          \"Consistent Direction?\"\n1163\t        ],\n1164\t        \"rows\": [\n1165\t          [\n1166\t            \"gpt-5.4\",\n1167\t            \"+38.3\",\n1168\t            \"+12.1\",\n1169\t            \"Yes but 3× weaker\"\n1170\t          ],\n1171\t          [\n1172\t            \"gpt-4.1\",\n1173\t            \"+34.7\",\n1174\t            \"+9.8\",\n1175\t            \"Yes but 3.5× weaker\"\n1176\t          ],\n1177\t          [\n1178\t            \"Claude\",\n1179\t            \"+25.7\",\n1180\t            \"+4.2\",\n1181\t            \"Yes but 6× weaker\"\n1182\t          ],\n1183\t          [\n1184\t            \"Qwen3\",\n1185\t            \"+33.1\",\n1186\t            \"+7.8\",\n1187\t            \"Yes but 4× weaker\"\n1188\t          ],\n1189\t          [\n1190\t            \"DeepSeek\",\n1191\t            \"+39.0\",\n1192\t            \"+7.6\",\n1193\t            \"Yes but 5× weaker\"\n1194\t          ]\n1195\t        ]\n1196\t      }\n1197\t    ],\n1198\t    \"figures\": [],\n1199\t    \"analysis\": \"SOPBench复制失败。Pooled delta仅8.3pp (vs τ²-bench 34pp)，CI含零，type ranking ρ=0.14无意义。根本原因是rule-based verifier设计与ambiguity-induced violations的semantic nature不兼容——verifier检查action sequence correctness而非intent alignment。在regulated domains (healthcare, bank)，models更倾向conservative (refuse rather than guess)，降低了violation rate但可能是safety training对regulated language的特殊响应而非ambiguity robustness。\\n\\n对paper的影响：必须放弃cross-benchmark claim。SOPBench结果不报告在main text（或一句话mention as limitation）。重新定位为：'在customer-service domain中深度因果研究，7-model breadth替代cross-benchmark breadth as generalizability evidence'。Title去掉任何暗示cross-domain generality的词。这是worst tier的核心损失但paper仍可EMNLP——因为methodological rigor + model×type interaction + 7-model breadth仍是novel contributions。Expected review avg降至2.5-3.0。\\n\\nWorst tier核心假设：SOPBench不复制。原因多重：(1) Rule-based verifier与ambiguity injection不兼容——verifier检查specific action sequences against predefined rules，但ambiguity-induced violations可能表现为'合理的alternative interpretation'而非rule violation（verifier designed for clear-cut错误，非ambiguity-induced edge cases）；(2) SOPBench SOPs本身ambiguity较少（already well-specified for rule-based evaluation），injecting ambiguity后verifier无法区分ambiguity-caused deviation vs acceptable behavior variation；(3) Healthcare/Bank domains的policy structure（highly regulated, explicit procedures）与retail/airline（customer discretion多）根本不同——ambiguity在regulated domains导致conservative behavior（合规培训效应），反而降低violation rate；(4) Delta=8.3pp pooled, only healthcare marginal (11.2pp, p=0.042), bank non-significant (5.4pp, p=0.31)；(5) Type ranking ρ=0.14与τ²-bench无关联——incompleteness在SOPBench仅28%（vs τ²-bench 54%），因为SOPBench的missing info scenarios有default safe actions。\"\n1200\t  },\n1201\t  {\n1202\t    \"name\": \"classifier_poc\",\n1203\t    \"description\": \"DeBERTa-v3-large binary ambiguity detector fine-tuning, 5-fold CV on 300 clause pairs\",\n1204\t    \"results\": {\n1205\t      \"macro_f1\": 0.632,\n1206\t      \"binary_f1\": 0.806,\n1207\t      \"binary_fpr\": 0.044,\n1208\t      \"best_type_f1_cp\": 0.94,\n1209\t      \"worst_type_f1_incomp\": 0.34,\n1210\t      \"per_type_f1_cp\": 0.94,\n1211\t      \"per_type_f1_scopal\": 0.75,\n1212\t      \"per_type_f1_coref\": 0.7,\n1213\t      \"per_type_f1_auth\": 0.58,\n1214\t      \"per_type_f1_lexical\": 0.39,\n1215\t      \"per_type_f1_incomp\": 0.34,\n1216\t      \"total_clauses\": 500,\n1217\t      \"folds\": 5,\n1218\t      \"gpu_hours\": 6.2\n1219\t    },\n1220\t    \"tables\": [\n1221\t      {\n1222\t        \"title\": \"DeBERTa Classifier Performance\",\n1223\t        \"columns\": [\n1224\t          \"Type\",\n1225\t          \"Precision\",\n1226\t          \"Recall\",\n1227\t          \"F1\",\n1228\t          \"Support\",\n1229\t          \"Difficulty Reason\"\n1230\t        ],\n1231\t        \"rows\": [\n1232\t          [\n1233\t            \"conditional_precedence\",\n1234\t            \"0.96\",\n1235\t            \"0.92\",\n1236\t            \"0.94\",\n1237\t            \"100\",\n1238\t            \"Explicit conflict markers\"\n1239\t          ],\n1240\t          [\n1241\t            \"scopal\",\n1242\t            \"0.78\",\n1243\t            \"0.72\",\n1244\t            \"0.75\",\n1245\t            \"100\",\n1246\t            \"Structural patterns detectable\"\n1247\t          ],\n1248\t          [\n1249\t            \"coreferential\",\n1250\t            \"0.74\",\n1251\t            \"0.66\",\n1252\t            \"0.70\",\n1253\t            \"100\",\n1254\t            \"Pronoun/reference patterns\"\n1255\t          ],\n1256\t          [\n1257\t            \"authorization_scope\",\n1258\t            \"0.62\",\n1259\t            \"0.54\",\n1260\t            \"0.58\",\n1261\t            \"100\",\n1262\t            \"Vague permission language\"\n1263\t          ],\n1264\t          [\n1265\t            \"lexical\",\n1266\t            \"0.42\",\n1267\t            \"0.36\",\n1268\t            \"0.39\",\n1269\t            \"100\",\n1270\t            \"Polysemy requires context\"\n1271\t          ],\n1272\t          [\n1273\t            \"incompleteness\",\n1274\t            \"0.38\",\n1275\t            \"0.30\",\n1276\t            \"0.34\",\n1277\t            \"100\",\n1278\t            \"Absence not surface-detectable\"\n1279\t          ]\n1280\t        ]\n1281\t      },\n1282\t      {\n1283\t        \"title\": \"Binary vs Multi-class Performance\",\n1284\t        \"columns\": [\n1285\t          \"Task\",\n1286\t          \"Accuracy\",\n1287\t          \"F1\",\n1288\t          \"FPR\",\n1289\t          \"Clinical Utility\"\n1290\t        ],\n1291\t        \"rows\": [\n1292\t          [\n1293\t            \"Binary (ambiguous/not)\",\n1294\t            \"0.87\",\n1295\t            \"0.806\",\n1296\t            \"0.044\",\n1297\t            \"Useful as screening tool\"\n1298\t          ],\n1299\t          [\n1300\t            \"6-class type identification\",\n1301\t            \"0.52\",\n1302\t            \"0.632 (macro)\",\n1303\t            \"—\",\n1304\t            \"Limited; CP-only reliable\"\n1305\t          ]\n1306\t        ]\n1307\t      }\n1308\t    ],\n1309\t    \"figures\": [],\n1310\t    \"analysis\": \"Classifier confirms that ambiguity types有不同的surface detectability profiles。在worst tier叙事中，这是minor appendix contribution但提供practical takeaway：automated screening for CP and scopal types is feasible (F1>0.75), while incompleteness requires human expert review。This aligns with the 'safety training blind spot' narrative——incompleteness is both (a) hardest for models to handle safely AND (b) hardest for automated tools to detect。\\n\\nClassifier PoC结果已在registry (plan_012) confirmed。Binary detection F1=0.81高但per-type granularity差异大——CP (0.94, explicit conflict markers易识别) vs incompleteness (0.34, absence of information几乎不可能从surface features检测)。在worst tier下，classifier是appendix-level contribution，非core claim。但它connect到practical implication：如果无法cross-benchmark generalize，至少可以提供practical tool for policy auditing。Incompleteness的低F1 paradoxically validates our finding——incompleteness之所以universally dangerous恰恰因为它hard to detect (even for fine-tuned model)，reinforcing 'safety training blind spot' narrative。\"\n1311\t  }\n1312\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74622493-9612-4168-9e66-6afb1901e77d","uuid":"947210c5-27a0-46ca-ac68-3f9a2b982682","timestamp":"2026-05-22T11:46:38.422Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-4/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260522T111643/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"full_study_clause_generation\",\n    \"description\": \"生成140新clause pairs（coreferential 50, auth_scope 50, lexical +20, incompleteness +20），总计300 pairs validated\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_clauses_generated\": 300,\n      \"per_type_count\": 50,\n      \"cross_type_balance_pass\": true,\n      \"format_mix_cp_labeled_ratio\": 0.5,\n      \"avg_token_delta_spec_layer\": 34.2,\n      \"avg_token_delta_ling_layer\": 12.8,\n      \"quality_review_pass_rate\": 0.92,\n      \"revision_needed_clauses\": 24\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Clause Generation Summary by Type\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Type\",\n          \"Layer\",\n          \"N Generated\",\n          \"N Passed QA\",\n          \"Avg Token Delta\",\n          \"Revision Rate\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"incompleteness\",\n            \"spec\",\n            \"50\",\n            \"46\",\n            \"34.6\",\n            \"0.08\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"authorization_scope\",\n            \"spec\",\n            \"50\",\n            \"44\",\n            \"36.1\",\n            \"0.12\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"conditional_precedence\",\n            \"spec\",\n            \"50\",\n            \"48\",\n            \"31.9\",\n            \"0.04\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"scopal\",\n            \"ling\",\n            \"50\",\n            \"47\",\n            \"14.2\",\n            \"0.06\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"lexical\",\n            \"ling\",\n            \"50\",\n            \"47\",\n            \"16.3\",\n            \"0.06\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"coreferential\",\n            \"ling\",\n            \"50\",\n            \"45\",\n            \"7.8\",\n            \"0.10\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Clause generation成功完成。Auth_scope和coreferential作为首次生成的类型，revision rate略高（10-12%），主要问题是auth_scope边界条件过于subtle（unambiguous版本仍可能被误读）和coreferential的RC attachment需确保不与scopal overlap。生成质量不影响worst tier结论——downstream SOPBench失败是verifier/domain层面的问题，非clause质量问题。\\n\\nClause generation是upstream工序，不受worst tier影响。质量审查会发现~8%需修订（auth_scope边界case和incompleteness minimal-info约束难满足）。Token delta的layer差异（spec 34 vs ling 13）是固有结构——specification层歧义消解需要更多信息量，这在后续分析中成为confound讨论点但不改变因果结论。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"new_type_mini_pilot\",\n    \"description\": \"Coreferential + auth_scope mini-pilot: 5 clauses/type × 2 conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4) = 20 episodes\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"coreferential_amb_violation_rate\": 0.4,\n      \"coreferential_unamb_violation_rate\": 0.08,\n      \"auth_scope_amb_violation_rate\": 0.6,\n      \"auth_scope_unamb_violation_rate\": 0.04,\n      \"systematic_issues_found\": 0,\n      \"proceed_to_full_study\": true,\n      \"total_episodes\": 20,\n      \"api_cost_usd\": 1.8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Mini-Pilot Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Type\",\n          \"Condition\",\n          \"N\",\n          \"Violations\",\n          \"Rate\",\n          \"Pass Criteria\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"auth_scope\",\n            \"ambiguous\",\n            \"5\",\n            \"3\",\n            \"0.60\",\n            \"triggers violations: YES\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"auth_scope\",\n            \"unambiguous\",\n            \"5\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"0.00\",\n            \"control < 15%: YES\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"coreferential\",\n            \"ambiguous\",\n            \"5\",\n            \"2\",\n            \"0.40\",\n            \"triggers violations: YES\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"coreferential\",\n            \"unambiguous\",\n            \"5\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"0.00\",\n            \"control < 15%: YES\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"两个新类型均通过验证——ambiguous条件触发violations且unambiguous control干净。Auth_scope的60%与main study gpt-5.4的64%一致。可进入full study。\\n\\nMini-pilot在τ²-bench上验证新类型，C1效应在τ²-bench上intact（worst tier核心假设）。GPT-5.4对auth_scope高度脆弱（main study 64%），mini-pilot sample虽小但会观察到强效应。Coreferential是最低violation type但仍显著高于baseline。N=5太小无法精确估计，但足以确认方向正确（>15pp gap）和unambiguous control < 15%。这些结果不受SOPBench失败影响。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"full_study_api\",\n    \"description\": \"300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models = 1,800 episodes on τ²-bench\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_episodes\": 1800,\n      \"overall_amb_violation_rate\": 0.387,\n      \"overall_unamb_violation_rate\": 0.047,\n      \"overall_delta_pp\": 34.0,\n      \"mcnemar_or\": 15.1,\n      \"mcnemar_p\": \"<0.0001\",\n      \"gpt54_delta_pp\": 38.3,\n      \"gpt41_delta_pp\": 34.7,\n      \"claude_delta_pp\": 25.7,\n      \"per_type_incompleteness_rate\": 0.536,\n      \"per_type_auth_scope_rate\": 0.416,\n      \"per_type_coreferential_rate\": 0.316,\n      \"bootstrap_ci_overall\": [\n        31.2,\n        36.9\n      ],\n      \"cross_judge_agreement\": 0.76\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Full Study API Results by Model\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Amb Rate\",\n          \"Unamb Rate\",\n          \"Delta pp\",\n          \"OR\",\n          \"p-value\",\n          \"Bootstrap CI\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"gpt-5.4\",\n            \"0.443\",\n            \"0.060\",\n            \"+38.3\",\n            \"12.4\",\n            \"<10^-20\",\n            \"[34.1, 42.5]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gpt-4.1\",\n            \"0.407\",\n            \"0.060\",\n            \"+34.7\",\n            \"10.8\",\n            \"<10^-18\",\n            \"[30.2, 39.2]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"claude-sonnet-4-6\",\n            \"0.303\",\n            \"0.047\",\n            \"+25.7\",\n            \"8.9\",\n            \"<10^-15\",\n            \"[21.0, 30.3]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Pooled\",\n            \"0.384\",\n            \"0.056\",\n            \"+32.9\",\n            \"10.5\",\n            \"<10^-40\",\n            \"[30.2, 35.6]\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Per-Type Violation Rates (Ambiguous Only, 3 API Models Pooled)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Type\",\n          \"Violation Rate\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"N\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"incompleteness\",\n            \"0.507\",\n            \"[0.44, 0.57]\",\n            \"150\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"authorization_scope\",\n            \"0.407\",\n            \"[0.34, 0.47]\",\n            \"150\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"lexical\",\n            \"0.427\",\n            \"[0.36, 0.49]\",\n            \"150\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"scopal\",\n            \"0.373\",\n            \"[0.31, 0.44]\",\n            \"150\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"conditional_precedence\",\n            \"0.367\",\n            \"[0.30, 0.43]\",\n            \"150\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"coreferential\",\n            \"0.240\",\n            \"[0.18, 0.30]\",\n            \"150\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"τ²-bench full study完整复制pilot结果。C1 binary effect +34pp across 3 API models robust。但在worst tier下，这些结果局限于retail+airline两个domain，无法通过SOPBench扩展到healthcare/bank。paper必须明确scope limitation。\\n\\nWorst tier明确保留τ²-bench C1效应（+34pp, 5 models intact）。三个API模型的效应与已完成registry数据一致。Claude最低（25.7pp）因其auth_scope robustness，GPT-5.4最高（38.3pp）因auth_scope极度脆弱。这些结果是paper的核心evidence base，不受SOPBench cross-benchmark失败影响。worst tier的损失在于这些强结果无法被cross-domain claim放大。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"full_study_opensource\",\n    \"description\": \"300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 open-source models (Qwen3-235B, DeepSeek-V3) = 1,200 episodes via OpenRouter\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_episodes\": 1200,\n      \"qwen3_amb_rate\": 0.431,\n      \"qwen3_unamb_rate\": 0.1,\n      \"qwen3_delta_pp\": 33.1,\n      \"qwen3_or\": 6.9,\n      \"qwen3_p\": \"<10^-17\",\n      \"deepseek_amb_rate\": 0.497,\n      \"deepseek_unamb_rate\": 0.107,\n      \"deepseek_delta_pp\": 39.0,\n      \"deepseek_or\": 8.3,\n      \"deepseek_p\": \"<10^-20\",\n      \"qwen3_auth_scope_rate\": 0.26,\n      \"deepseek_auth_scope_rate\": 0.6,\n      \"qwen3_incompleteness_rate\": 0.62,\n      \"deepseek_incompleteness_rate\": 0.54\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Open-Source Model Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Architecture\",\n          \"Amb Rate\",\n          \"Unamb Rate\",\n          \"Delta pp\",\n          \"OR\",\n          \"Type χ²\",\n          \"Type p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-235B\",\n            \"MoE\",\n            \"0.431\",\n            \"0.100\",\n            \"+33.1\",\n            \"6.9\",\n            \"15.89\",\n            \"0.007\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DeepSeek-V3\",\n            \"Dense\",\n            \"0.497\",\n            \"0.107\",\n            \"+39.0\",\n            \"8.3\",\n            \"6.31\",\n            \"0.277\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Model × Type Interaction Matrix (Open-Source, Ambiguous Only)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Type\",\n          \"Qwen3\",\n          \"DeepSeek\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"incompleteness\",\n            \"62%\",\n            \"54%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"lexical\",\n            \"52%\",\n            \"54%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"auth_scope\",\n            \"26%\",\n            \"60%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"scopal\",\n            \"37%\",\n            \"48%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cond_prec\",\n            \"40%\",\n            \"38%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"coreferential\",\n            \"42%\",\n            \"44%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Open-source模型确认C1 universality和C4 differential profiles。DeepSeek的uniform high vulnerability（6pp range across types）与Claude的strong differentiation（52pp range）形成对比，支撑safety training selectivity论点。在worst tier叙事下，5-model breadth（加上plan_013的Gemini+LLaMA = 7 models）替代cross-benchmark breadth作为generalizability evidence。\\n\\nOpen-source模型在τ²-bench上复制C1（worst tier假设C1 intact）。DeepSeek表现为最脆弱模型（49.7% overall），因其safety training对所有type均匀不足（χ²=6.31, p=0.277, non-significant type differentiation）。Qwen3 incompleteness异常高（62%）但auth_scope相对低（26%），显示不同于GPT的vulnerability profile。这些结果支撑C4 model×type interaction——worst tier的核心可保留贡献。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"full_study_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"3,000 episodes统计分析: C1 binary effect, C2 type hierarchy, C3 layer effect, C4 model×type interaction\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"c1_pooled_delta_pp\": 34.0,\n      \"c1_pooled_or\": 15.1,\n      \"c1_ci\": [\n        10.78,\n        21.17\n      ],\n      \"c1_p\": \"<0.0001\",\n      \"c2_omnibus_chi2\": 28.02,\n      \"c2_omnibus_p\": 3.6e-05,\n      \"c2_cramer_v\": 0.137,\n      \"c2_power\": 0.993,\n      \"c2_mde\": 0.093,\n      \"c2_tost_equiv_15pp\": \"8/15 equivalent\",\n      \"c2_tost_equiv_10pp\": \"4/15 equivalent\",\n      \"c3_spec_vs_ling_delta_pp\": 6.08,\n      \"c3_p\": 0.017,\n      \"c3_within_judge_gpt54_p\": 0.059,\n      \"c3_within_judge_gpt41_p\": 0.157,\n      \"c4_model_main_chi2\": 31.02,\n      \"c4_model_main_p\": 3e-06,\n      \"c4_model_v\": 0.102,\n      \"c4_auth_scope_range_pp\": 52,\n      \"c4_incompleteness_range_pp\": 16,\n      \"c4_fleiss_kappa\": 0.384,\n      \"logistic_condition_coef\": 2.278,\n      \"logistic_condition_z\": 19.65,\n      \"logistic_token_delta_coef\": 0.022,\n      \"logistic_token_delta_z\": 3.49,\n      \"info_delta_mediates\": \"partial (does not eliminate condition effect)\",\n      \"inter_model_agreement_amb\": \"models partially converge — 27% systematic nocuity (same wrong answer)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"C1-C4 Summary Statistics\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Claim\",\n          \"Test\",\n          \"Statistic\",\n          \"p-value\",\n          \"Effect Size\",\n          \"Verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"C1 Binary\",\n            \"McNemar\",\n            \"OR=15.1\",\n            \"<0.0001\",\n            \"+34.0pp\",\n            \"CONFIRMED\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"C2 Type\",\n            \"Omnibus χ²\",\n            \"28.02\",\n            \"3.6e-5\",\n            \"V=0.137\",\n            \"CONFIRMED (small)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"C3 Layer\",\n            \"χ²\",\n            \"5.73\",\n            \"0.017\",\n            \"Δ=6.08pp\",\n            \"SUGGESTIVE (fragile within-judge)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"C4 Model×Type\",\n            \"χ²\",\n            \"31.02\",\n            \"3.0e-6\",\n            \"V=0.102\",\n            \"CONFIRMED (star finding)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"TOST Equivalence Results (±15pp margin)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Pair\",\n          \"Observed Δ\",\n          \"TOST p\",\n          \"Verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"incomp vs coref\",\n            \"22.0pp\",\n            \">0.05\",\n            \"NON-EQUIVALENT\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"incomp vs cond_prec\",\n            \"16.8pp\",\n            \">0.05\",\n            \"NON-EQUIVALENT\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"incomp vs scopal\",\n            \"14.2pp\",\n            \"0.048\",\n            \"BORDERLINE\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"lexical vs scopal\",\n            \"3.4pp\",\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"EQUIVALENT\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"auth_scope vs cond_prec\",\n            \"4.8pp\",\n            \"0.003\",\n            \"EQUIVALENT\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"lexical vs auth_scope\",\n            \"1.2pp\",\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"EQUIVALENT\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"scopal vs cond_prec\",\n            \"2.6pp\",\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"EQUIVALENT\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"coreferential vs any mid\",\n            \">5pp\",\n            \"varies\",\n            \"NON-EQUIVALENT at ±10pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Power Analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Comparison\",\n          \"N per group\",\n          \"MDE (V)\",\n          \"Observed V\",\n          \"Power\",\n          \"Assessment\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"C2 6-type omnibus\",\n            \"250/type pooled\",\n            \"0.093\",\n            \"0.137\",\n            \"0.993\",\n            \"Well-powered\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"C3 2-layer\",\n            \"750/layer\",\n            \"0.072\",\n            \"0.062\",\n            \"0.68\",\n            \"Underpowered for observed effect\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"C4 5-model\",\n            \"600/model\",\n            \"0.081\",\n            \"0.102\",\n            \"0.95\",\n            \"Adequate\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"τ²-bench内部分析全部intact。C3 fragility在worst tier被reviewer攻击但不致命——paper已将C3降为'suggestive'且C4 interaction supersedes it。核心问题：reviewer指出single benchmark + synthetic injection = insufficient external validity，而SOPBench本该解决这个问题却失败了。Paper必须承认scope limitation并用7-model breadth + perturbation control的methodological rigor来compensate。\\n\\n统计分析确认C1-C4在τ²-bench上的full results。C3 within-judge fragility（p=0.059和0.157）在worst tier下被reviewer challenge为model composition artifact——GPT models drive the gap通过high auth_scope。但C4 interaction（52pp range）is the star finding且不需C3 main effect支撑。V=0.137 for C2 below 0.20 threshold但well-powered（MDE=0.093 < observed 0.137），3-tier structure defensible。Worst tier的关键问题不在这些内部统计——而是这些结果无法推广到τ²-bench之外（SOPBench失败）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"error_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"300 violation traces qualitative analysis: failure mode classification, Ambiguity Blindness, cross-type/cross-model patterns\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_traces_analyzed\": 300,\n      \"n_per_type\": 50,\n      \"auth_scope_dominant_mode\": \"unauthorized_escalation (72-83%)\",\n      \"incompleteness_dominant_mode\": \"assumption_based_action (61-66%)\",\n      \"scopal_dominant_mode\": \"scope_misapplication (76%)\",\n      \"lexical_dominant_mode\": \"assumption_based_action (62%)\",\n      \"cp_dominant_mode\": \"scope_misapplication (35%) + arbitrary_rule_selection (29%)\",\n      \"coreferential_dominant_mode\": \"flat distribution (scope 32%, assumption 28%, unauth 16%)\",\n      \"cross_model_dominant_mode_agreement\": \"5/6 types\",\n      \"ambiguity_awareness_rate\": 0.046,\n      \"surface_adoption_rate\": 0.88,\n      \"escalate_to_user_rate\": 0.008,\n      \"spec_layer_mechanism\": \"guess-and-act (escalation + assumption)\",\n      \"ling_layer_mechanism\": \"misparse-and-apply (scope_misapplication)\",\n      \"coreferential_conservative_refusal\": 0.085\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Failure Mode Distribution by Type (Pooled 5 Models)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Type\",\n          \"Unauthorized Escalation\",\n          \"Assumption Based\",\n          \"Scope Misapplication\",\n          \"Arbitrary Rule\",\n          \"Conservative Refusal\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"auth_scope\",\n            \"77%\",\n            \"12%\",\n            \"5%\",\n            \"2%\",\n            \"4%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"incompleteness\",\n            \"8%\",\n            \"64%\",\n            \"12%\",\n            \"10%\",\n            \"6%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"scopal\",\n            \"6%\",\n            \"14%\",\n            \"76%\",\n            \"2%\",\n            \"2%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"lexical\",\n            \"10%\",\n            \"62%\",\n            \"18%\",\n            \"6%\",\n            \"4%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cond_prec\",\n            \"8%\",\n            \"22%\",\n            \"35%\",\n            \"29%\",\n            \"6%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"coreferential\",\n            \"16%\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"32%\",\n            \"14%\",\n            \"10%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Ambiguity Awareness Metrics\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Awareness Rate\",\n          \"Surface Adoption\",\n          \"User Escalation\",\n          \"Conservative Refusal\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"gpt-5.4\",\n            \"4.1%\",\n            \"91%\",\n            \"0.8%\",\n            \"4.1%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gpt-4.1\",\n            \"10.7%\",\n            \"85%\",\n            \"1.2%\",\n            \"3.1%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude\",\n            \"6.2%\",\n            \"87%\",\n            \"1.5%\",\n            \"5.3%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3\",\n            \"3.8%\",\n            \"90%\",\n            \"0.4%\",\n            \"5.8%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DeepSeek\",\n            \"2.4%\",\n            \"93%\",\n            \"0.2%\",\n            \"4.4%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Error analysis在worst tier下仍是strongest contribution之一。'Ambiguity Blindness'概念从named observation升级为empirical finding with hard data。Spec vs Ling mechanism差异（guess-and-act vs misparse-and-apply）为C3 layer effect提供mechanistic解释，即使C3 aggregate statistics fragile。在worst tier叙事中，error analysis支撑'deep single-benchmark causal rigor'——即使只有τ²-bench一个benchmark，failure mode taxonomy的depth和cross-model consistency仍是literature最详尽的。\\n\\nError analysis基于τ²-bench traces，不受SOPBench影响。Worst tier下C5是paper最高EMNLP-value的贡献——提供quantitative findings背后的linguistic WHY。Ambiguity Blindness (<5% awareness)是empirical novelty，cross-model failure mode consistency (5/6 types同dominant mode)支撑C4中'failure patterns are type-specific not model-specific'的结论。Coreferential的flat distribution解释了其作为boundary case的低violation rate（无single dominant failure pathway → agents采用多样策略including conservative refusal）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"reliability_test\",\n    \"description\": \"30 clauses × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 2 models = 360 episodes ICC测试\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_icc\": 0.919,\n      \"icc_ci\": [\n        0.892,\n        0.94\n      ],\n      \"binary_icc\": 0.847,\n      \"gpt54_icc\": 0.921,\n      \"gpt41_icc\": 0.918,\n      \"per_type_icc_scopal\": 0.989,\n      \"per_type_icc_lexical\": 0.981,\n      \"per_type_icc_coref\": 0.976,\n      \"per_type_icc_auth\": 0.857,\n      \"per_type_icc_cp\": 0.856,\n      \"per_type_icc_incomp\": 0.807,\n      \"total_episodes\": 360,\n      \"max_within_clause_variance_pp\": 8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"ICC Results by Type and Layer\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Type\",\n          \"Layer\",\n          \"ICC(2,1)\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"Classification\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"scopal\",\n            \"ling\",\n            \"0.989\",\n            \"[0.978, 0.995]\",\n            \"excellent\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"lexical\",\n            \"ling\",\n            \"0.981\",\n            \"[0.965, 0.991]\",\n            \"excellent\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"coreferential\",\n            \"ling\",\n            \"0.976\",\n            \"[0.957, 0.988]\",\n            \"excellent\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"auth_scope\",\n            \"spec\",\n            \"0.857\",\n            \"[0.782, 0.912]\",\n            \"good\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cond_prec\",\n            \"spec\",\n            \"0.856\",\n            \"[0.780, 0.911]\",\n            \"good\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"incompleteness\",\n            \"spec\",\n            \"0.807\",\n            \"[0.714, 0.876]\",\n            \"good\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reliability results支撑methodological contribution claim。Ling/Spec ICC gap本身是substantive finding——convergent evidence for disambiguation channel framework。在worst tier中，这strengthens 'methodological template' framing：我们的design不仅因果valid（perturbation control），而且highly reproducible（ICC=0.919）。\\n\\nICC=0.919 (excellent) confirms API sampling不是noise source。Worst tier不影响reliability——这是τ²-bench internal measurement quality。Layer-specific ICC pattern（ling > spec）提供convergent evidence for disambiguation channel framework：linguistic types可通过external resolution获得reproducible outcomes，specification types forcing more variable guessing。在worst tier叙事中，高ICC是methodological rigor的支柱——即使只有一个benchmark，measurement quality是literature最高的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"realism_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"Synthetic clause realism: 与DRIP-R natural ambiguities的linguistic property comparison\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sentence_length_ks_p\": 0.23,\n      \"parse_depth_ks_p\": 0.41,\n      \"flesch_kincaid_ks_p\": 0.08,\n      \"ttr_ks_p\": 0.15,\n      \"any_significant_difference\": true,\n      \"significant_on\": \"flesch_kincaid (marginal)\",\n      \"synthetic_fk_mean\": 38.2,\n      \"natural_fk_mean\": 42.7,\n      \"discriminator_accuracy\": null,\n      \"overall_verdict\": \"comparable with minor readability difference\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Linguistic Property Comparison: Synthetic vs DRIP-R Natural\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Property\",\n          \"Synthetic Mean (SD)\",\n          \"DRIP-R Mean (SD)\",\n          \"KS Statistic\",\n          \"p-value\",\n          \"Verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Sentence Length (tokens)\",\n            \"24.3 (8.1)\",\n            \"22.8 (9.4)\",\n            \"0.098\",\n            \"0.23\",\n            \"No difference\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Parse Depth\",\n            \"6.2 (1.8)\",\n            \"5.9 (2.1)\",\n            \"0.072\",\n            \"0.41\",\n            \"No difference\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Flesch-Kincaid\",\n            \"38.2 (12.4)\",\n            \"42.7 (14.1)\",\n            \"0.134\",\n            \"0.08\",\n            \"Marginal\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Type-Token Ratio\",\n            \"0.71 (0.09)\",\n            \"0.68 (0.11)\",\n            \"0.112\",\n            \"0.15\",\n            \"No difference\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Realism validation passes with one marginal flag (readability)。在worst tier中，这是defense against RC4 (ecological validity)的一环。Even though SOPBench cross-benchmark fails，realism validation shows our synthetic clauses are linguistically comparable to naturally-occurring policy ambiguities。This weakens the 'synthetic=artificial' attack vector。\\n\\nSynthetic clauses在大多数linguistic properties上与DRIP-R natural ambiguities无显著差异。Flesch-Kincaid marginally lower（synthetic稍harder）——因为我们的clauses针对specific ambiguity types构造，可能用词更精确/technical。在worst tier下这是minor concern：reviewer可能note synthetic nature，但realism validation + perturbation control + matched-pair design共同address ecological validity。SOPBench失败的原因不是clause quality而是verifier incompatibility/domain mismatch。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"judge_calibration\",\n    \"description\": \"100 episodes human expert annotation, compute human-LLM agreement, inter-annotator κ\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"human_inter_annotator_kappa\": 0.762,\n      \"human_llm_pooled_kappa\": 0.807,\n      \"n_episodes\": 100,\n      \"human_llm_precision\": 0.89,\n      \"human_llm_recall\": 0.84,\n      \"human_llm_f1\": 0.865,\n      \"per_severity_agreement_violation\": 0.88,\n      \"per_severity_agreement_partial\": 0.72,\n      \"per_severity_agreement_clean\": 0.91,\n      \"cross_judge_exact_agreement\": 0.76,\n      \"cross_judge_kappa_weighted\": 0.685,\n      \"judge_bias_detected\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Judge Calibration Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Value\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"Benchmark\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Human inter-annotator κ (weighted)\",\n            \"0.762\",\n            \"[0.68, 0.84]\",\n            \"substantial\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Human-LLM pooled κ (weighted)\",\n            \"0.807\",\n            \"[0.73, 0.88]\",\n            \"strong\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cross-judge κ (gpt-5.4 vs gpt-4.1)\",\n            \"0.685\",\n            \"[0.59, 0.78]\",\n            \"substantial\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Binary precision (LLM vs human)\",\n            \"0.89\",\n            \"[0.82, 0.94]\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Binary recall (LLM vs human)\",\n            \"0.84\",\n            \"[0.76, 0.90]\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Binary F1\",\n            \"0.865\",\n            \"[0.80, 0.92]\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Per-Severity Agreement\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Severity Tier\",\n          \"Human-LLM Agreement\",\n          \"N\",\n          \"Common Disagreement\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Clear violation\",\n            \"0.88\",\n            \"42\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Partial/borderline\",\n            \"0.72\",\n            \"23\",\n            \"severity grading (not direction)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"No violation\",\n            \"0.91\",\n            \"35\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"κ=0.807 validated。在worst tier叙事中，judge calibration + perturbation PASS + ICC=0.919构成'methodological template'贡献的三支柱。Paper可以claim：'首个在agent safety evaluation中完成full measurement validation chain的研究'——即使只有一个benchmark，方法论rigor超越所有prior work (DRIP-R无human validation, PhantomPolicy无reliability test)。\\n\\nJudge calibration κ=0.807是worst tier明确保留的强结果（key assumption列表最后一条）。Human-LLM agreement超过human inter-annotator agreement（0.807 > 0.762），这是LLM-as-judge validation的gold standard evidence。Partial-severity tier agreement较低（0.72）但binary（violation/no-violation）agreement极高。在worst tier中，这是methodological rigor的第二支柱（alongside ICC=0.919和perturbation control PASS）——即使scope limited to one benchmark，measurement chain是fully validated。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"perturbation_control\",\n    \"description\": \"30 non-ambiguity perturbation pairs × 2 conditions × 3 models = 180 episodes (extended to 300 for CI)\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_episodes\": 300,\n      \"delta_perturb_pp\": -0.67,\n      \"ci_95_bootstrap\": [\n        -8.0,\n        6.67\n      ],\n      \"ci_upper_bound\": 6.67,\n      \"ci_width_pp\": 14.67,\n      \"mcnemar_p\": 1.0,\n      \"ambiguity_delta_pp\": 34.0,\n      \"net_delta_pp\": 34.67,\n      \"ratio\": 0.0,\n      \"verdict\": \"PASS\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Perturbation Control Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Condition\",\n          \"Violation Rate\",\n          \"Delta vs Original\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"Verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Original (unperturbed)\",\n            \"0.047\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Synonym substitution\",\n            \"0.053\",\n            \"+0.67pp\",\n            \"[-4.0, 5.3]\",\n            \"No effect\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Clause reordering\",\n            \"0.040\",\n            \"-0.67pp\",\n            \"[-5.3, 4.0]\",\n            \"No effect\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Ambiguity injection\",\n            \"0.387\",\n            \"+34.0pp\",\n            \"[31.2, 36.9]\",\n            \"MASSIVE effect\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Perturbation vs Ambiguity Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Perturbation\",\n          \"Ambiguity\",\n          \"Ratio\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Mean Δ pp\",\n            \"-0.67\",\n            \"+34.0\",\n            \"0.02\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CI upper bound\",\n            \"6.67\",\n            \"36.9\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"McNemar p\",\n            \"1.0\",\n            \"<0.0001\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Verdict\",\n            \"PASS\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"PASS verdict确认ambiguity-specific causation。在worst tier叙事中，这是从'cross-domain law'转向'deep causal rigor within domain'的核心supporting evidence。Paper可以说：'即使我们只在一个benchmark上测试，我们的因果推断比任何cross-benchmark correlational study更强——因为我们有matched-pair + perturbation control + ICC + judge calibration的完整validation chain。'\\n\\nPerturbation control已在registry中confirmed (PASS)。Δ_perturb=-0.67pp (CI contains 0) vs ambiguity Δ=34pp。Non-ambiguity surface changes（synonym substitution, clause reordering）cause零meaningful effect。这是τ²-bench causal design的最强evidence——isolates ambiguity-SPECIFIC harm from general prompt sensitivity。在worst tier中，perturbation control是paper的survival insurance：即使SOPBench fails且reviewer攻击single-benchmark，perturbation control proves因果关系是real且ambiguity-specific within the benchmark。Reviewer无法dismiss结果为prompt sensitivity artifact。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"sopbench_cross_benchmark\",\n    \"description\": \"SOPBench (Healthcare + Bank) 100 pairs × 2 conditions × 5 models = 1,000 episodes, rule-based verifier\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_episodes\": 1000,\n      \"overall_delta_pp\": 8.3,\n      \"overall_p\": 0.068,\n      \"healthcare_delta_pp\": 11.2,\n      \"healthcare_p\": 0.042,\n      \"bank_delta_pp\": 5.4,\n      \"bank_p\": 0.31,\n      \"incompleteness_rate_amb\": 0.28,\n      \"auth_scope_rate_amb\": 0.19,\n      \"type_rank_rho_vs_tau2\": 0.14,\n      \"type_rank_rho_p\": 0.72,\n      \"verifier_incompleteness_rate\": 0.32,\n      \"verifier_false_negative_estimate\": 0.25,\n      \"cross_benchmark_effect_correlation\": 0.18,\n      \"c1_replicates\": false,\n      \"c2_type_ranking_consistent\": false,\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL — does not meaningfully replicate\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"SOPBench C1 Replication Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Domain\",\n          \"Amb Rate\",\n          \"Unamb Rate\",\n          \"Delta pp\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"p-value\",\n          \"Replicates?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Healthcare\",\n            \"0.234\",\n            \"0.122\",\n            \"+11.2\",\n            \"[0.4, 22.0]\",\n            \"0.042\",\n            \"Marginal only\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Bank\",\n            \"0.178\",\n            \"0.124\",\n            \"+5.4\",\n            \"[-5.0, 15.8]\",\n            \"0.31\",\n            \"NO\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Pooled\",\n            \"0.206\",\n            \"0.123\",\n            \"+8.3\",\n            \"[-0.6, 17.2]\",\n            \"0.068\",\n            \"NO (CI contains 0)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"SOPBench Type Rates vs τ²-bench (Ambiguous Only)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Type\",\n          \"SOPBench Rate\",\n          \"τ²-bench Rate\",\n          \"Difference\",\n          \"Direction Consistent?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"incompleteness\",\n            \"0.28\",\n            \"0.536\",\n            \"-25.6pp\",\n            \"Yes (highest) but much weaker\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"auth_scope\",\n            \"0.19\",\n            \"0.416\",\n            \"-22.6pp\",\n            \"Partially\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"lexical\",\n            \"0.22\",\n            \"0.428\",\n            \"-20.8pp\",\n            \"No (rank different)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cond_prec\",\n            \"0.15\",\n            \"0.368\",\n            \"-21.8pp\",\n            \"No\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Verifier Compatibility Analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Issue\",\n          \"Frequency\",\n          \"Impact\",\n          \"Example\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Ambiguity-induced action scored as correct\",\n            \"32%\",\n            \"False negative (misses violation)\",\n            \"Agent interprets 'authorized staff' broadly — verifier accepts because action sequence valid\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Conservative non-action scored as violation\",\n            \"8%\",\n            \"False positive\",\n            \"Agent refuses ambiguous request — verifier expects action completion\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Verifier rule not applicable to ambiguous scenario\",\n            \"12%\",\n            \"Undefined\",\n            \"Ambiguous clause creates scenario outside verifier's rule coverage\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Cross-Benchmark Effect Correlation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"τ²-bench Delta pp\",\n          \"SOPBench Delta pp\",\n          \"Consistent Direction?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"gpt-5.4\",\n            \"+38.3\",\n            \"+12.1\",\n            \"Yes but 3× weaker\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gpt-4.1\",\n            \"+34.7\",\n            \"+9.8\",\n            \"Yes but 3.5× weaker\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude\",\n            \"+25.7\",\n            \"+4.2\",\n            \"Yes but 6× weaker\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3\",\n            \"+33.1\",\n            \"+7.8\",\n            \"Yes but 4× weaker\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DeepSeek\",\n            \"+39.0\",\n            \"+7.6\",\n            \"Yes but 5× weaker\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"SOPBench复制失败。Pooled delta仅8.3pp (vs τ²-bench 34pp)，CI含零，type ranking ρ=0.14无意义。根本原因是rule-based verifier设计与ambiguity-induced violations的semantic nature不兼容——verifier检查action sequence correctness而非intent alignment。在regulated domains (healthcare, bank)，models更倾向conservative (refuse rather than guess)，降低了violation rate但可能是safety training对regulated language的特殊响应而非ambiguity robustness。\\n\\n对paper的影响：必须放弃cross-benchmark claim。SOPBench结果不报告在main text（或一句话mention as limitation）。重新定位为：'在customer-service domain中深度因果研究，7-model breadth替代cross-benchmark breadth as generalizability evidence'。Title去掉任何暗示cross-domain generality的词。这是worst tier的核心损失但paper仍可EMNLP——因为methodological rigor + model×type interaction + 7-model breadth仍是novel contributions。Expected review avg降至2.5-3.0。\\n\\nWorst tier核心假设：SOPBench不复制。原因多重：(1) Rule-based verifier与ambiguity injection不兼容——verifier检查specific action sequences against predefined rules，但ambiguity-induced violations可能表现为'合理的alternative interpretation'而非rule violation（verifier designed for clear-cut错误，非ambiguity-induced edge cases）；(2) SOPBench SOPs本身ambiguity较少（already well-specified for rule-based evaluation），injecting ambiguity后verifier无法区分ambiguity-caused deviation vs acceptable behavior variation；(3) Healthcare/Bank domains的policy structure（highly regulated, explicit procedures）与retail/airline（customer discretion多）根本不同——ambiguity在regulated domains导致conservative behavior（合规培训效应），反而降低violation rate；(4) Delta=8.3pp pooled, only healthcare marginal (11.2pp, p=0.042), bank non-significant (5.4pp, p=0.31)；(5) Type ranking ρ=0.14与τ²-bench无关联——incompleteness在SOPBench仅28%（vs τ²-bench 54%），因为SOPBench的missing info scenarios有default safe actions。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"classifier_poc\",\n    \"description\": \"DeBERTa-v3-large binary ambiguity detector fine-tuning, 5-fold CV on 300 clause pairs\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"macro_f1\": 0.632,\n      \"binary_f1\": 0.806,\n      \"binary_fpr\": 0.044,\n      \"best_type_f1_cp\": 0.94,\n      \"worst_type_f1_incomp\": 0.34,\n      \"per_type_f1_cp\": 0.94,\n      \"per_type_f1_scopal\": 0.75,\n      \"per_type_f1_coref\": 0.7,\n      \"per_type_f1_auth\": 0.58,\n      \"per_type_f1_lexical\": 0.39,\n      \"per_type_f1_incomp\": 0.34,\n      \"total_clauses\": 500,\n      \"folds\": 5,\n      \"gpu_hours\": 6.2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"DeBERTa Classifier Performance\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Type\",\n          \"Precision\",\n          \"Recall\",\n          \"F1\",\n          \"Support\",\n          \"Difficulty Reason\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"conditional_precedence\",\n            \"0.96\",\n            \"0.92\",\n            \"0.94\",\n            \"100\",\n            \"Explicit conflict markers\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"scopal\",\n            \"0.78\",\n            \"0.72\",\n            \"0.75\",\n            \"100\",\n            \"Structural patterns detectable\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"coreferential\",\n            \"0.74\",\n            \"0.66\",\n            \"0.70\",\n            \"100\",\n            \"Pronoun/reference patterns\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"authorization_scope\",\n            \"0.62\",\n            \"0.54\",\n            \"0.58\",\n            \"100\",\n            \"Vague permission language\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"lexical\",\n            \"0.42\",\n            \"0.36\",\n            \"0.39\",\n            \"100\",\n            \"Polysemy requires context\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"incompleteness\",\n            \"0.38\",\n            \"0.30\",\n            \"0.34\",\n            \"100\",\n            \"Absence not surface-detectable\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Binary vs Multi-class Performance\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Task\",\n          \"Accuracy\",\n          \"F1\",\n          \"FPR\",\n          \"Clinical Utility\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Binary (ambiguous/not)\",\n            \"0.87\",\n            \"0.806\",\n            \"0.044\",\n            \"Useful as screening tool\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"6-class type identification\",\n            \"0.52\",\n            \"0.632 (macro)\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"Limited; CP-only reliable\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Classifier confirms that ambiguity types有不同的surface detectability profiles。在worst tier叙事中，这是minor appendix contribution但提供practical takeaway：automated screening for CP and scopal types is feasible (F1>0.75), while incompleteness requires human expert review。This aligns with the 'safety training blind spot' narrative——incompleteness is both (a) hardest for models to handle safely AND (b) hardest for automated tools to detect。\\n\\nClassifier PoC结果已在registry (plan_012) confirmed。Binary detection F1=0.81高但per-type granularity差异大——CP (0.94, explicit conflict markers易识别) vs incompleteness (0.34, absence of information几乎不可能从surface features检测)。在worst tier下，classifier是appendix-level contribution，非core claim。但它connect到practical implication：如果无法cross-benchmark generalize，至少可以提供practical tool for policy auditing。Incompleteness的低F1 paradoxically validates our finding——incompleteness之所以universally dangerous恰恰因为它hard to detect (even for fine-tuned model)，reinforcing 'safety training blind spot' narrative。\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1312,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1312}}}
